  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On the grassland the lake is tranquil and crystal-like, with bent pointed ends and a wider middle that give it the crescent shape.",
      "chapters": [
        459
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "On the grassland the lake is fifteen thousand li long and five thousand li wide. The two ends are bent and pointed while the middle is wide, giving a crescent moon shape. The water is tranquil and gives off a crystal-like sparkle. Aquatic plants are plentiful. Horseshoe trees surround the lake in a sparse woodland, and living beings there include three-horned rhinos, water wolves, and dragon-fish.",
      "chapters": [
        459
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grey-white stone pillars stand in stone forests beside the lake.",
      "chapters": [
        461
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ge tribe camps around those horseshoe trees; the lakeside holds many dangers, among them a larger water wolf group, a three-horned rhino group, a group of a thousand mutated beasts, and a worm group that can number in the hundreds of thousands or more.",
      "chapters": [
        461
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shore-and-waters",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ge_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Crescent lake has the most water wolves among the wolf kinds found there, with turtleback wolves, night wolves, and wind wolves also present.",
      "chapters": [
        485
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shore-and-waters",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "While small and mid-sized tribes leave for the heroes assembly, Ge tribe stays for a time among the aquatic plants and digests battle gains.",
      "chapters": [
        485
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tribes-beside-the-lake",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later only Ge tribe remains at crescent lake; Fang Yuan then orders the tribe to onion valley before they go on to Yu Tian.",
      "chapters": [
        496
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tribes-beside-the-lake",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_yu_tian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Immortals at rank six arrive above the lake’s center and treat Lang Ya blessed land as hidden there, expecting an earthly calamity.",
      "chapters": [
        459
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lang-ya-near-the-lake",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "East along the lakeside from Ge tribe’s camp, away from the tribe’s sight, a stone forest stands beside crescent lake as the passage Ma Hong Yun used to enter Lang Ya blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        461
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lang-ya-near-the-lake",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ma_hong_yun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fixed Immortal Travel brings him beside the lake again, leftover snow from the blizzard disaster still piles on the shore while dragonfish leap from the water. He and Tai Bai Yun Sheng search for the purple stone tree passage into Lang Ya blessed land; the changed ground blocks a direct teleport to that tree, so he uses a cave Tai Bai Yun Sheng once dug beside the lake.",
      "chapters": [
        660
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lang-ya-near-the-lake",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_fixed_immortal_travel",
        "char_tai_bai_yun_sheng",
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier, Lang Ya blessed land was near Crescent Lake, but it relocated after Shadow Sect’s attack.",
      "chapters": [
        1048
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-relocation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_shadow_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When the land spirit first relocated from crescent lake to Loose Tail Ridge, he kept the new seat from Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        1763
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-relocation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_loose_tail_ridge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya land spirit later explains the old placement: the area near Crescent Lake has many water path dao marks and refinement path dao marks, which suited the killer move immortal tribulation tempering aperture.",
      "chapters": [
        1051
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-relocation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Calamities drawn by that move most often brought water path and refinement path marks into the aperture.",
      "chapters": [
        2042
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-relocation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
